.TITLE "mount"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Attaches a filesystem to the system hierarchy. It makes the contents of __storage devices__ or network shares accessible at a specific mount point.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**mount**
Lists all currently mounted filesystems.
> 

**mount -u -o rw /**
Remounts the root filesystem with read-write permissions.
> __-u__ update flag | __-o__ options flag | __rw__ read-write option | __/__ root path

**mount -t msdos /dev/disk2s1 /Volumes/USB**
Mounts a specific device with a specified filesystem type.
> __-t__ type flag | __/dev/disk2s1__ device path | __/Volumes/USB__ mount point

.DIV "SUMMARY"
On modern macOS, many mounting tasks are handled automatically by the Disk Management framework. The __mount__ command remains essential for low-level system administration and manual control over filesystem options.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:umount** **mac:diskutil**

